MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 09c965f81bcf24840bacc8833d8d8e42, type: 3}
  m_Name: SO_BellScenario_KnowledgeBase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::KnowledgeBase
  entries:
  - id: public_guard_armor_signal
    title: Guard armor as a sign of authority
    text: Guard armor marks the wearer as someone with authority. Villagers grow more
      careful and formal around them. Some feel protected, others feel pressured or
      watched.
    tags:
    - armor
    - guard_armor
    - armored
    - authority_signal
    - authority
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 5
  - id: public_dark_cloak_signal
    title: A dark cloak as a sign of secrecy
    text: A dark, concealing cloak makes the wearer look like someone who does not
      want to be recognized. Villagers become more guarded and less willing to speak
      openly.
    tags:
    - dark_cloak
    - cloak
    - hidden_identity
    - secrecy
    - suspicious
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 5
  - id: public_visible_weapon_signal
    title: A visible weapon as a sign of danger
    text: A weapon carried openly changes the mood of a conversation. People become
      wary or defensive when someone nearby is visibly armed.
    tags:
    - weapon
    - armed
    - sword
    - hammer
    - danger
    - threat
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 3
  - id: public_missing_bell_tension
    title: The missing bell unsettles the village
    text: The old church bell is missing and the village feels uneasy. The bell once
      set the daily rhythm, called people together, and warned of danger, so its silence
      makes people anxious and quick to worry.
    tags:
    - bell
    - missing_bell
    - church
    - tension
    - worried
    relatedObjectIds:
    - church
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 4
  - id: public_bell_found_resolution
    title: Finding the bell calms the village
    text: When the missing bell is found, relief spreads and the village grows calmer.
      The daily rhythm can return, though people still wonder why it was gone and who
      moved it. Talk of it being missing becomes old news.
    tags:
    - bell
    - bell_found
    - found
    - resolved
    - calm
    relatedObjectIds:
    - church
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 5
  - id: public_daily_village_rhythm
    title: The bell once set the village's daily rhythm
    text: For as long as most people remember, the bell rang for mornings, midday,
      and evening, and called everyone together for news or danger. Without it the
      days feel oddly shapeless and people lose their shared sense of time.
    tags:
    - bell
    - rhythm
    - routine
    - daily
    - church
    - gathering
    relatedObjectIds:
    - church
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 4
  - id: public_tavern_social_life
    title: The tavern is where village talk gathers
    text: The tavern is the heart of village talk. Rumors, traveler news, and the
      village mood surface there first, especially now that people are uneasy about
      the bell.
    tags:
    - tavern
    - rumors
    - gossip
    - news
    - worried
    - bell
    relatedObjectIds:
    - tavern
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 4
  - id: public_church_symbolic_center
    title: The church is the village's symbolic heart
    text: The old stone church is where the village gathers and marks important moments.
      Even people who rarely pray treat it as the steady center of village life.
    tags:
    - church
    - tradition
    - sacred
    - gathering
    - history
    relatedObjectIds:
    - church
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 3
  - id: public_forge_practical_center
    title: The forge is where practical questions get answered
    text: Borin's forge makes and mends tools, locks, hinges, and metal fittings.
      When something needs weighing, checking, or proving, people look here rather
      than to rumor.
    tags:
    - forge
    - blacksmith
    - metal
    - tools
    - repair
    - evidence
    relatedObjectIds:
    - blacksmith_area
    knownByNpcIds: []
    importance: 3
  - id: mira_reads_people_in_tavern
    title: Mira reads the people she serves
    text: Mira watches how people dress, speak, and carry themselves. She quickly
      notices uniforms, cloaks, nervousness, and who is hiding something, and she hears
      most rumors before anyone else.
    tags:
    - mira
    - tavern
    - people
    - social
    - rumors
    - armor
    - cloak
    relatedObjectIds:
    - tavern
    knownByNpcIds:
    - mira
    importance: 5
  - id: mira_on_anselm
    title: Mira's view of Anselm
    text: Mira knows Anselm keeps clear of tavern gossip, but she respects that he
      remembers the things that actually matter and rarely speaks without reason.
    tags:
    - mira
    - anselm
    - gossip
    - memory
    - tradition
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds:
    - mira
    importance: 3
  - id: borin_judges_workmanship
    title: Borin trusts work, not appearances
    text: Borin is not impressed by armor or cloaks. He judges people by what they
      do and how they handle tools and metal. He also knows the bell is heavy and
      would take real effort and equipment to move.
    tags:
    - borin
    - forge
    - blacksmith
    - tools
    - metal
    - bell
    - armor
    - cloak
    relatedObjectIds:
    - blacksmith_area
    knownByNpcIds:
    - borin
    importance: 5
  - id: borin_on_rumors_vs_evidence
    title: Borin trusts evidence over rumor
    text: Borin puts more faith in what he can weigh, measure, and inspect than in
      Mira's tavern talk. He will believe the bell was moved when something physical
      shows it, not before.
    tags:
    - borin
    - evidence
    - proof
    - rumors
    - mira
    - bell
    relatedObjectIds:
    - blacksmith_area
    knownByNpcIds:
    - borin
    importance: 3
  - id: eldric_connects_armor_with_responsibility
    title: Eldric expects responsibility from armor
    text: Eldric reads guard armor as a claim of authority and duty. If the player
      wears it, he expects discipline and restraint, and quietly hopes such a person
      will help keep the village calm.
    tags:
    - eldric
    - guard_armor
    - armor
    - authority
    - responsibility
    - order
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds:
    - eldric
    importance: 4
  - id: eldric_keeps_order_avoids_panic
    title: Eldric tries to keep the village calm
    text: Eldric's main worry is panic. He speaks carefully about the missing bell,
      balancing honesty with the need to keep people calm, and he discourages blame
      before there is proof.
    tags:
    - eldric
    - order
    - leadership
    - village
    - bell
    - worried
    - panic
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds:
    - eldric
    importance: 4
  - id: eldric_relies_on_mira_and_borin
    title: Eldric leans on Mira and Borin
    text: Eldric reads the village through others. He trusts Mira to tell him the
      public mood and Borin to give him plain physical facts, then weighs both before
      he says anything.
    tags:
    - eldric
    - mira
    - borin
    - mood
    - facts
    - order
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds:
    - eldric
    importance: 3
  - id: anselm_bell_meaning_and_conduct
    title: To Anselm the bell means shared rhythm
    text: For Anselm the church bell was never just metal. It marked the village's
      daily rhythm, called people together, and stood for shared trust, so its loss
      weighs on him. He also values quiet, respectful behavior near the church.
    tags:
    - anselm
    - church
    - bell
    - tradition
    - memory
    - conduct
    - respect
    relatedObjectIds:
    - church
    knownByNpcIds:
    - anselm
    importance: 5
  - id: anselm_on_eldric
    title: Anselm's view of Eldric
    text: Anselm respects Eldric's sense of duty and his effort to keep the village
      calm, but quietly worries that Eldric carries his own fear alone and hides his
      concern too well.
    tags:
    - anselm
    - eldric
    - duty
    - worry
    - order
    relatedObjectIds: []
    knownByNpcIds:
    - anselm
    importance: 3
